    mission: { situation: ['You are Emma. Your tutor reads Ren\'s follow-up message, then plays Claire during a short call. Tell Claire about the agreed visit and how you and Ren will keep work separate.', 'あなたはエマ役です。講師はレンの追加の連絡を読んでから、短い電話でクレア役になります。確定した京都の予定と、仕事を分ける方法をクレアに伝えましょう。'], task: ['Listen for the day, time, meeting point, and what to bring. Explain what will happen if Ren is delayed, and distinguish the date from an exhibition planning meeting.', '曜日、時間、待ち合わせ場所、持ち物を聞き取りましょう。レンが遅れる場合の対応と、デートが展示会の打ち合わせではないことを説明しましょう。'], roles: ['Claire', 'Emma'], text: '<p>Saturday at two is confirmed. Let\'s meet outside the small cafe with the green awning in Gion. Bring your camera; I would like to see the streets you photograph. If my train is delayed, I will message you before our meeting time. We can leave work decisions for Monday\'s team meeting.</p>', lines: ['Emma, when are you meeting Ren in Kyoto?', 'How will you recognise the meeting place?', 'What will you bring, and why?', 'What will he do if his train is delayed?', 'Is this a work meeting to decide the exhibition designs?', 'When will the team discuss work decisions?'], evidence: 'Saturday2, outside small cafe/green awning/Gion, camera for streets, message before meeting if delayed, date not work approval, work Monday team meeting. Assess listening facts separately from minor grammar. The cafe description is fictional practice evidence, not a real venue recommendation.', useful: ['We have agreed to meet ...', 'The cafe has ...', 'I need to bring ...', 'If he is delayed, he will ...', 'This is not ...', 'We will discuss work on ...'] },
    topics: [['CLEAR EXPECTATIONS', ['How can you explain what matters to you?', 'How can you check another person\'s expectations?', 'What could you say when a plan changes?']], ['WORK AND FREE TIME', ['How could you keep work topics for a work meeting?', 'What would you enjoy on a day off?', 'How can you suggest changing the topic politely?']], ['MEETING SOMEONE', ['Which details make a meeting point clear?', 'What should you do if you are late?', 'How can you confirm a plan briefly?']]],
    trivia: ['"Start fresh" means make a new beginning. It does not literally mean forgetting what happened. Someone can start fresh while still explaining expectations and taking responsibility for earlier choices.', 'start fresh は新たに始めるという意味で、過去を文字どおり忘れることではありません。新しく始めるときにも、望むことを伝え、以前の選択に責任を持つことはできます。'], triviaQuestion: ['Does "start fresh" necessarily mean pretending the past never happened?', 'No. It means making a new beginning.'],
